,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":549.359530278,"data":"--- Problem tech_vieta_formulas [algebra.polynomials.vieta_formulas] ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":549.359532397,"data":"Triggers: polynomial coefficients and need symmetric expressions of roots, sum/product of roots without finding them, system of equations with symmetric variables as roots of auxiliary polynomial\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":549.359536327,"data":"Technique: Vieta formulas: for poly a_n*x^n+...+a_0 with roots r_i, e_k(roots) = (-1)^k * a_{n-k}/a_n. For quadratic x^2-Sx+P: r1+r2=S, r1*r2=P. For cubic x^3-Sx^2+Px-Q: sum=S, pairwise=P, product=Q. Use to build auxiliary polynomial from symmetric system.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":549.359541688,"data":"Question: If a+b+c=6, ab+bc+ca=11, abc=6, find a^2+b^2+c^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":549.359543934,"data":"Answer: a,b,c are roots of t^3-6t^2+11t-6=0 = (t-1)(t-2)(t-3). But we can also compute directly: a^2+b^2+c^2 = (a+b+c)^2 - 2(ab+bc+ca) = 36-22 = 14. This is the fundamental use of Vieta: express any symmetric function of roots in terms of elementary symmetric polynomials (which equal polynomial coefficients up to sign). Newton sums extend this to power sums recursively.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":549.359546953,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":549.35954858,"data":"[END NOTES]\n"}
